==History==
'''Bilibili Gaming'''  was formed in December 2017, through the acquisition of the [[I May]] ''League of Legends'' roster by '''Bilibili''', a Chinese video sharing website. <ref name="c9 history">{{cite web|url=https://www.espn.com/esports/story/_/id/22083613/the-league-legends-offseason-report-cards-lpl|title=The League of Legends offseason report cards -- LPL|author=Kelsey Moser|publisher=ESPN|date=2018-01-13|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> In 2019, the organization expanded to ''Overwatch'', but disbanded in 2022. Nevertheless, in February 2023, they announced their ''Valorant'' team. 

The ''League of Legends'' team won two consecutive Demacia Cups in [[Demacia_Cup/2022|2022]] and [[Demacia_Cup/2023|2023]], and got second place at the [[LPL/2023/Spring|LPL Spring 2023]] and [[Mid-Season_Invitational/2023|Mid-Season Invitational 2023]].


