==History==
'''FlyQuest''' debuted in the [[LCS/North_America/Spring/2017|NA LCS Spring 2017 Season]] after buying the spot of [[Cloud9 Challenger]] which was promoted to the LCS through the [[LCS/North_America/Spring/2017/Promotion|promotion tournament]]. <ref name="NA LCS Offseason, Scheduling, and more">{{cite web |url=http://www.lolesports.com/en_US/articles/na-lcs-offseason-scheduling-and-more|title=NA LCS Offseason, Scheduling, and more|author= |date=2017-01-06|publisher=[http://www.lolesports.com/en_US LoL Esports] |language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> Their first roster was formed as 4 of the [[Cloud9 Challenger]] players joined, [[Balls]], [[Hai]], [[Altec]] and [[LemonNation]]. Joining them was former [[Team Liquid]] player and analyst [[Moon]] to finalize the roster. In its first split, the team qualified to the playoffs, where it finished 4th, winning over [[Counter Logic Gaming]] in the quarterfinal while losing to [[Team SoloMid]] in the semifinal and to [[Phoenix1]] in the 3rd place match.

Since then, '''FlyQuest''' has become won an LCS title, finished second 3 times, attended MSI, and competed at Worlds twice, most notably taking [[Gen.G Esports]] to 5 games in the [[World_Championship/2024|2024 World Championship]].

