==History==
===Merger with Rogue (2022-2023)===
On October 6, 2022, '''KOI''' revealed they merged with '''[[Rogue]]''', causing KOI to replace [[Rogue]] in [[LEC]] 2023 season.<ref name="KOI 2023"> {{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/KOI/status/1578110739381985280|title=KOI 2023|date=2022-10-06|author=KOI}}</ref><ref name="KOI x Rogue"> {{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/KOI/status/1578111285010780160|title=Unimos fuerzas con Rogue y conquistaremos el mundo como KOI en 2023|date=2022-10-06|author=KOI}}</ref><ref name="KOI LEC"> {{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/KOI/status/1578113965539950608|title=El comienzo de una nueva era|date=2022-10-06|author=KOI}}</ref><ref name="Rogue X KOI"> {{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/Rogue/status/1578108813613625345|title=ROGUE AND KOI JOINING FORCES, We're ready to take the next step as an organization alongside KOI|date=2022-10-06|author=[[Rogue]]}}</ref> The partership ended on November 22th, 2023.<ref name="rogue back">{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/RoguexOfficial/status/1727379082218725745|title=Motivated by our fans who still feel rogue at heart, ReKtGlobal reclaims its brand identity as Rogue.|date=2023-11-22|author=[[Rogue]]}}</ref>

===Merger with MAD Lions (2024)===
In January 2024 [[wikipedia:OverActive_Media|OverActive Media]] announced the acquisition of  '''KOI''' and '''[[Movistar Riders|Movistar Riders]]''', merging it with '''[[MAD Lions|MAD Lions]]''' to form a single organization. During 2024 KOI functioned as the academy team of [[MAD Lions|MAD Lions KOI]]. With the [[MAD Lions]] name retiring, KOI returned to the LEC for the 2025 season. <ref name="MAD KOI">{{cite web |url=https://x.com/MovistarKOI_en/status/1865066596793806895|title=One identity. We are Movistar KOI.|author=[[Movistar KOI]]|date=2024-12-06}}</ref>

